## Webview Preloader Architecture

The standard webview preloader at `out/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html` provides the foundation for all webviews (Composer, terminal, extensions, etc.).

### Origin Validation

```html
<!-- Webview validates origin using SHA-256 hash -->
<!-- Hash = base32(sha256(parentOrigin + ':' + webviewOrigin)) -->
<!-- Iframe hostname must match {hash} or {hash}.{domain} -->
```

This prevents unauthorized cross-origin injection of webview content.

### Service Worker

```javascript
// out/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/service-worker.js
self.addEventListener('install', () => {
  self.skipWaiting();
});

self.addEventListener('activate', () => {
  clients.claim();
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  event.respondWith(
    caches.open('webview').then((cache) => {
      return cache.match(event.request).then((response) => {
        return response || fetch(event.request).then((networkResponse) => {
          cache.put(event.request, networkResponse.clone());
          return networkResponse;
        });
      });
    })
  );
});
```

### Dual-Frame Technique

The webview uses an active/pending frame swap mechanism:

1. **active-frame**: Currently visible webview content
2. **pending-frame**: New content loading in background
3. When pending-frame loads, frames are swapped atomically
4. Prevents flickering during navigation

### vsCodeApi Bridge

```javascript
// Injected into every webview via acquireVsCodeApi()
function acquireVsCodeApi() {
  let ready = false;
  let state = undefined;
  const _postMessage = (msg) => {
    if (!ready) throw new Error('Webview not ready');
    window.parent.postMessage({
      type: 'did-post-message',
      value: msg
    }, '*');
  };
  return {
    postMessage(msg) {
      _postMessage(msg);
    },
    setState(s) {
      state = s;
      _postMessage({ type: 'did-set-state', value: s });
    },
    getState() {
      return state;
    },
    _setReady(r) {
      ready = r;
    }
  };
}
```

