## Glass UI Mode

Cursor includes a secondary UI mode called **Glass UI**, introduced as an alternative to the standard workbench.

### Activation

| CLI Flag | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `--glass` | Enable Glass UI mode |
| `--classic` | Disable Glass UI, use classic workbench (default) |

### Differences from Classic Workbench

| Aspect | Classic Workbench | Glass UI |
|--------|------------------|----------|
| **Socket Error Handling** | Disconnection is fatal | Non-fatal for background composer |
| **Reconnection** | Immediate | Grace period of 360 attempts |
| **Background Composer** | Same reconnection logic | Special `isBackgroundComposerConnection()` check |
| **Remote Authority** | Standard | Mapped via `gn()` function |
| **Code Location** | `out/vs/workbench/` | `out/vs/glass/` |

### Glass Code Location

```
out/vs/glass/
├── glass-main.js        # Glass entry point
├── glass.css            # Glass-specific styles
└── [various components] # Glass UI components
```

Glass UI is checked in the main process:

```javascript
// When isGlass is true, socket disconnection errors are not fatal
if (isGlass && error.type === 'CursorSocketTransient') {
  // Non-fatal: allow reconnection
  return;
}
// Disposal only happens if NOT glass or permanent failure
if (isGlass !== true) {
  socket.dispose();
}
```

